{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1488032-the-tremere\u2019s-\u201cseventh-watchtower\u201d","id":1488032,"title":"The Tremere\u2019s \u201cSeventh Watchtower\u201d","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-26T08:51:51-07:00","id":1488032,"title":"The Tremere\u2019s \u201cSeventh Watchtower\u201d","content":"It apparently existed in the material realm, but then was somehow...lost.<br /> <br /> What <i>was</i> Chur? An Atlantean ruin they ascribed more meaning to than was originally intended? A piece of the Lower Depths jutting into the Fallen World? A fragment of the Time Before? A Watchtower from a parallel timeline?<br /> <br /> Let\u2019s be creative, here. What <i>was</i> Chur in <i>your</i> games?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12219,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","user":"Demigod Beast","date":". 09-28-2022, 02:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T12:27:15-07:00","id":1488070,"title":"","content":"The echo of the Watchtowers in the material, just like a ghost is to the original person.<br /> <br /> When Chur was destroyed, it lost its Anchor. Ghosts fall to the Underworld to be consumed, the ghost of the Watchtowers fell to the Lower Depths to be emptied.<br /> <br /> Having some degree of sentience, it sought out the Awakened to willingly bind themselves to it, forging chains of sympathy to keep it from falling to oblivion. Now it wages a constant war to get enough power from Awakened souls to pull itself back up to the material, but the Depths hunger. Those that bind themselves to the Watchtower have that ravenous hunger attempt to consume them as well.<br /> <br /> Preta are those who were overwhelmed by it, Tremere are afflicted by its hunger more intensely as they learn to draw more power from it. <br /> <br /> The Watchtower is being burned of all meaning by the Lower Depths, the subtle Arcana in the soul act as a buffer and only those with Gnosis have the supernatural tolerance to stand any chance of surviving metaphysical contact with it.<br /> <br /> So maybe the Tremere have a point and maybe it can become a more accessible Watchtower, but would the price really be worth it ? How many souls would need to be sacrificed to recover it and what else would be needed ? What is to prevent it from falling to oblivion again ? So many questions, the eldest liches still seek the answers, either due to sunken cost or forlorn hope","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-26-2022, 11:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T12:29:55-07:00","id":1488072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KaiserAfini</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1488032-the-tremere\u2019s-\u201cseventh-watchtower\u201d?p=1488070#post1488070\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The echo of the Watchtowers in the material, just like a ghost is to the original person.<br /> <br /> When Chur was destroyed, it lost its Anchor. Ghosts fall to the Underworld to be consumed, the ghost of the Watchtowers fell to the Lower Depths to be emptied.<br /> <br /> Having some degree of sentience, it sought out the Awakened to willingly bind themselves to it, forging chains of sympathy to keep it from falling to oblivion. Now it wages a constant war to get enough power from Awakened souls to pull itself back up to the material, but the Depths hunger. Those that bind themselves to the Watchtower have that ravenous hunger attempt to consume them as well.<br /> <br /> Preta are those who were overwhelmed by it, Tremere are afflicted by its hunger more intesely as they learn to draw more power from it. <br /> <br /> The Watchtower is being burned of all meaning by the Lower Depths, the subtle Arcana in the soul act as a buffer and only those with Gnosis have the supernatural tolerance to stand any chance of surviving metaphysical contact with it.<br /> <br /> So maybe the Tremere have a point and maybe it can become a more accessible Watchtower, but would the price really be worth it ? How many souls would need to be sacrificed to recover it and what else would be needed ? What is to prevent it from falling to oblivion again ? So many questions, the eldest liches still seek the answers, either due to sunken cost or forlorn hope</div> </div> </div> </div>This...is fricking <i>awesome</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T12:31:07-07:00","id":1488073,"title":"","content":"Did it have anything resembling inhabitants, prior to the Tremere showing up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T14:50:50-07:00","id":1488095,"title":"","content":"I would say it acted like a Verge for all mechanical purposes and the &quot;heart&quot; of Chur acting like a &quot;soul stone&quot; that holds it together, like a bizarre Demesne. <br /> <br /> The being inside could come in two groups, odd since there are only subtle Arcana to work with, but ghosts are always off from the original, given time.<br /> <br /> The first are Zeitgeists, spirits of notable times in history. You have ones for times like the Summer of Love or the Age of Enlightenment, you have the mercurial ones for the Golden Age of Piracy and you have the brutal chaos of the Pangean era.<br /> <br /> The seconds are the Thesians, a Root People made of the Subtle Arcana, reflections of the visitors, people in their lives and sometimes ones they do not know, a product of Fate's foreshadowing. Interacting with them can be enlightening, like talking to a reflection through a different lens. It can also be eerie, sometimes drawing visitors to trials about the metaphysics of identity. After all, how can one know which is the real Ship of Theseus ?<br /> <br /> So you must be asking, what happened to its keystone, the Artifact that held it in place ? It's the Metatron Clock, one of the most prized Artifacts of the Mysterium (found on their core book). Its why they have such a terrible time researching it, the clues now are in some thaumavoric realm of horror where reality corrodes, even they want nothing to do with that. Naturally, its a secret to all but the most senior member. Yep, the blood dragon's heart is a quantum clockwork Artifact, his species had the first archmasters of magic for a reason.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":24280,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","user":"KaiserAfini","date":". 07-26-2022, 05:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T14:53:36-07:00","id":1488096,"title":"","content":"Are the Exarchs involved, in your version of Chur? Or is it a distorted copy of the real thing, without any Exarchs and Oracles involved at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T15:10:46-07:00","id":1488097,"title":"","content":"As a half-goof/half-hook, I'll just point out that Transylvania is moderately close to the Eastern Carpathians, that the Lower Depths are characterized as both hungry and infernal, and that the largest Tremere house in the modern day is derived from a Legacy whose powers contemporary Sleepers believed came from the Devil, and let you draw what conclusions you may from that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T15:11:33-07:00","id":1488098,"title":"","content":"I added a few extra details at the end of the previous post that were missing.<br /> <br /> The Exarchs were tangentially involved, I see it as the the blood dragon's alternative system to the Watchtowers. No need slowly and carefully reach across the Supernal. But he failed to consider having a Watchtower in the Fallen meant mortals would be free to make a mess of it.<br /> <br /> Well at least those are the outlines, the finer details, like what happened to him, are things that I leave open to figure out based on the chronicle's themes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>New experiences are the font of creativity, when seeking inspiration, break your routine.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1278855-the-agathos-kai-sophos-a-acanthus-legacy-of-strategists\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Agathos Kai Sophos</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Acanthus Legacy of strategists (Mind/Time)</span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1360568-the-szary-stra%C5%BCnik-an-obrimos-legacy-of-scholars-of-the-glyphs-of-fate\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#1155CC\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">The Szary Stra\u017cnik</span></span></a><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">, an Obrimos Legacy whose invisible hands guide through the Glyphs of Fate (Fate/Prime)</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24280-kaiserafini","name":"KaiserAfini","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24280_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T15:20:45-07:00","id":1488101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1488032-the-tremere\u2019s-\u201cseventh-watchtower\u201d?p=1488097#post1488097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As a half-goof/half-hook, I'll just point out that Transylvania is moderately close to the Eastern Carpathians, that the Lower Depths are characterized as both hungry and infernal, and that the largest Tremere house in the modern day is derived from a Legacy whose powers contemporary Sleepers believed came from the Devil, and let you draw what conclusions you may from that.</div> </div> </div> </div>KUPALA!!! BEHOLD THE FIRE-FLOWER OF LIBERATION!!!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T14:46:58-07:00","id":1488215,"title":"","content":"Anybody else?<br /> <br /> As for myself, after some degree of thought, in my games, Chur as a Watchtower is a complete fabrication. Though Chur existed and was insanely magically powerful, it was no Watchtower. It was a thorn jutting up from the Lower Depths, dredged up by some unknown archmaster in a timeline That no longer exists in a futile plot to overthrow the Exarchs.<br /> <br /> Chur wasn\u2019t destroyed, it just <i>shifted</i> to a new location. The Tremere are a bunch of supernatural drug addicts who are making use of something that portends great danger to the Fallen World.<br /> <br /> Chur\u2019s \u2018native\u2019 inhabitants\u2014-before the Tremere destroyed them all\u2014-were strangely beautiful origami puzzles of flesh and mathematics equations that cannot exist. Some of these things still survive, albeit in the Lower Depth Chur is part of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}